<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="RISCV:LE:64:default">
<!--
    GH-9203: a late conditional-branch simplification inserts a MULTIEQUAL input
    p-code op into the wrong (loop) block, manifesting as a malformed do/while
    whose body holds a spurious constant assignment.

    ActionConditionalConst (coreaction.cc) propagates a value known-constant along
    a conditional out-edge.  When the value reaches a MULTIEQUAL on a disconnected
    incoming edge, handlePhiNodes() materializes the constant as a fresh COPY op
    placed at the BOTTOM of that edge's predecessor block and rewires the MULTIEQUAL
    input to it.  Here the predecessor is a LOOP block, so the (tmp = 0) COPY lands
    inside the loop body and is re-executed every iteration:

      iVar1 = 7;
      do {
        iVar1 = iVar1 + -1;
        xVar2 = 0;             // out-of-place: belongs outside the loop
      } while (iVar1 != 0);

    Stage model: S3 "simplification-quiescence" (WHERE a propagated constant is
    materialized).  The kuna fix is an anchor-edit at the decision point in
    handlePhiNodes(), always on: when the MULTIEQUAL edge predecessor block has
    a looping in-edge (bl->hasLoopIn()), decline to place the constant COPY
    there and leave the MULTIEQUAL input intact.

    Assert #1 keys on "= 0;" with min=max=0: the loop body never carries the
    out-of-place (xVar2 = 0;).  Assert #2 keys on "do {" with min=max=1: the
    loop structure itself is preserved (we did not destroy control flow).

    repro: kprobe.py (arch RISCV:LE:64:default) over the bytechunk below, "print C".
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x0">
397106fc4af022f826f42e8411492400ef0030602a8909ed414585471d471d8f7dff4274a274e2704a85027921618280130910fafdb7
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x0" name="FUN_0"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <!-- returndup (DIV-54 default-on) splits this function's shared epilogue, which moves
       the loop-body COPY this test watches; off to isolate the placement guard. -->
  <com>option returndup off</com>
  <com>lo fu FUN_0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH9203 #1: no const COPY in the loop body" min="0" max="0">= 0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH9203 #2: loop structure preserved" min="1" max="1">do \{</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
